# Copy this file to .env and fill in your keys. NEVER commit .env.

# --- Voice / TTS (optional) ---
# If unset, Easel will use its built-in / local fallback for V1 smoke test.
VOICE_PROVIDER=
VOICE_API_KEY=
VOICE_ID=

# --- Easel (after bootstrap, easel doctor will show what is needed) ---
EASEL_PORT=8765

# --- MiniMax M Plan (subscription) ---
# Credential. Resolved once per invocation and bound to both the billing gate and the
# provider transport, so the key that was authorised is the key that is used.
# MINIMAX_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=
# Falls back to MINIMAX_API_KEY, then to the official CLI's own ~/.mmx/config.json.

# Provider host. Endpoint URLs are deliberately NOT committed (AGENTS.md section 8),
# so the host is supplied here. There is no built-in default: the wrong regional host
# answers with an invalid-api-key status, which looks like a broken credential.
# The host actually used is recorded in every receipt as `base_url_host`.
# CONTENTOPS_MINIMAX_BASE_URL=
# MINIMAX_VOICE_CLONE_BASE_URL=      # overrides the above for the clone capability

# Raw cloned voice id. Personal, so it is never committed. Only its SHA256 appears in
# tracked receipts.
# MINIMAX_FOUNDER_VOICE_ID=

# Pay-as-you-go API Key for the M2.2 two-key clone route.
#
# Deliberately has NO fallback chain. The Subscription Key was refused once by
# /v1/voice_clone with status_code 2061 (the plan does not cover 快速复刻), so the
# clone must go through a pay-as-you-go key while narration stays on the plan. If this
# variable fell back to the Subscription Key the clone would be re-sent on the plan
# that already refused it.
#
# Used for exactly two calls: one upload and one clone. Never for TTS -- pay-as-you-go
# TTS is forbidden outright and has no ceiling in the codebase.
#
# Create at 账户管理 > 接口密钥 in the official console. No recharge is needed to
# create the key.
# MINIMAX_CLONE_KEY=

# --- Optional: OpenClaw gateway (NOT used by V1) ---
# OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_URL=
# OPENCLAW_API_KEY=

# --- Logging ---
LOG_LEVEL=INFO